Local changes for Outpost Luna (desktop/vendor/libarc):
- src/arc_nft2_ort.c: plain_session() reads the RNNT .onnx files into memory and uses CreateSessionFromArray (as the
  encoder already does), so no file path crosses the ONNX Runtime API (ORTCHAR_T is wchar_t on Windows).
- ort_loader.c (new): OrtGetApiBase() is resolved at run time from the ONNX Runtime library set with
  arc_ort_set_library() (declared in include/arc.h) or ARC_ORT_LIB, so libarc links no ONNX Runtime. The app ships a
  pinned Microsoft release build of it next to libarc (onnxruntime.lock.json, downloaded and sha256-checked by
  cmake/vendor_onnxruntime.cmake; MIT License, its LICENSE and ThirdPartyNotices.txt copied alongside). The C API
  version used is 23 (ONNX Runtime 1.23 headers); newer runtimes serve older API versions.
- include/arc.h, src/arc_api.c: ARC_ABI_VERSION / ARC_VERSION and arc_abi_version() / arc_version(), with the bump
  rules in arc.h; the Python binding is generated from arc.h (model_server/tools/gen_bindings.py).
- compat/win/: tiny pthread mutex / mmap shims for Windows builds of arc_nft2_ort.c, and arc_u8io.h / arc_u8io.c
  (force-included on Windows): fopen / open / rename / remove take UTF-8 paths through _wfopen / _wopen (binary) /
  MoveFileExW / _wremove, so a model folder under a non-ASCII user name opens.

third_party/onnxruntime/include: ONNX Runtime 1.23.2 C API headers (Microsoft, MIT License, third_party/onnxruntime/LICENSE).

The model weights (WhissleAI/arc-transcriber-space, nft2/) are NOT here: the app downloads them on first run with their
own LICENSE and NOTICE (desktop/assets.manifest.json).
